# Text files are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks files out with CRLF, and anything that parses a file's exact
# bytes reads different content than it does anywhere else. That is not hypothetical here: the guard
# on published skills tests `text.startsWith('---\n')` to find YAML frontmatter, which is false for
# `---\r\n`, so every shipped skill read as "no frontmatter — the CLI will skip it" and CI went red
# on Windows only. Three separate tests parse markdown frontmatter this way.
#
# LF is also what these files ARE. The skills, the docs and the changelog are published artifacts
# read by other tools; a CRLF copy on one contributor's disk is a local accident, not the content.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary and leaves it alone, so images and fonts are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary, named explicitly so no heuristic has to decide.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.icns binary

# Windows-only scripts that must keep CRLF to run at all.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The changelog is append-at-the-top, so every open PR edits the same lines and each merge
# invalidates every other PR. Measured 2026-08-23: five contributor PRs all reported CONFLICTING
# against main, and every one of them conflicted on THIS FILE ALONE — their code merged cleanly.
# With 20+ PRs open that makes the merge order strictly serial and hands each contributor a
# conflict badge they did not cause.
#
# `union` keeps BOTH sides of an overlapping hunk instead of raising a conflict, which is exactly
# the resolution a maintainer performs by hand here: two entries, both kept. It cannot silently
# drop an entry — the failure mode is duplicated or out-of-order lines, which is visible in review
# and harmless to fix, unlike a lost changelog line nobody notices.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to source: union merge on code produces text that compiles and means
# something nobody wrote. It belongs on append-only prose and nowhere else.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
